Package: s3-fleet
Version: 0.0.0-replaced-by-makefile
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: replaced-by-makefile
Recommends: openssh-client
Maintainer: Jérôme Poulin <jeromepoulin@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/ticpu/s3-fleet
Description: SSH host fleet kept in S3, with pinned host keys and labels
 s3-fleet keeps a fleet of SSH hosts as one YAML document in an S3 bucket:
 each host's pinned host keys and labels, plus fleet-wide attributes. The
 endpoint is discovered through DNS, reads need no credentials, and every
 write is conditional so concurrent edits are never lost. It lists hosts by
 label for scripts, exports known_hosts lines, and runs ssh trusting only
 the pinned keys.
